## 5. NEW SCREENS (plain surface, accurate underneath, one clear action)

**Screen A — Store / Recommended for You** `app/(main)/(store)/index.tsx`
- Top section: "Recommended from your plan" — only items whose `linked_finding` matches this user's triggered interventions. This is the personalised, high-relevance part.
- Below: "Full catalog" — browsable, still each via `<ClinicalTerm>` (plain name big, clinical name underneath).
- Every card shows price and an "Add" button that runs `canPurchase()` first.

**Screen B — Product Detail** `app/(main)/(store)/product.tsx`
- Full `<ClinicalTerm>` block, plain description, the exact clinical basis, price, and any safety state (consent needed / interaction check / iodine block) shown in plain language.
- "Add to cart" or the appropriate blocked/needs-check state.

**Screen C — Cart** `app/(main)/(store)/cart.tsx`
- Line items, quantities, running total (display only — real total comes from the Edge Function).
- Re-runs `canPurchase()` on each item at load in case the user's status changed.
- "Checkout" button.

**Screen D — Checkout & Payment** `app/(main)/(store)/checkout.tsx`
- Calls `create-payment-intent`, opens Stripe Payment Sheet.
- Clear states: processing, success, failure — never a blank screen. On failure, the cart is preserved.

**Screen E — Orders / Tracking** `app/(main)/(orders)/index.tsx`
- List of past orders with payment + fulfilment status in plain words ("Paid — being prepared", "Shipped", "Sample kit on the way").
- Tap into an order for its line items and status timeline.

Update Home so the journey tracker now ends at: Questionnaire → Tests → Results → Plan → **Order & track** → Follow-up.

