## 7. PHASE 3 ERROR-PROOFING ADDITIONS

- [ ] Prices are ALWAYS computed server-side; the app never sends an amount to charge.
- [ ] Stripe secret key is only in the Edge Function secret; app holds only the publishable key.
- [ ] Payment failure preserves the cart and shows a friendly retry, never a blank screen.
- [ ] `canPurchase()` runs on every add-to-cart AND again at cart load (status can change between).
- [ ] Consent-required products cannot be bought without the consent row.
- [ ] Iodine hard-stop and interaction flags block/flag at purchase, in plain language.
- [ ] Draft (un-reviewed) interventions are not purchasable.
- [ ] Order totals are snapshotted into `order_items` so later price changes don't rewrite history.
- [ ] SQL went in the SQL editor; Edge Function TypeScript went in Edge Functions.

